# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Vercel build-upload exclusions (docs/VERCEL_PROJECTS.md §6)
#
# These paths are tracked in git but never needed by a Vercel build or at
# runtime: CI-only, sandbox-only, or documentation-only. Excluding them keeps
# every deployment's source upload small (the ~19 MB of OCR assets under
# public/tesseract is runtime-required and intentionally NOT excluded).
#
# Keep in sync with tsconfig.json `exclude` (tests, mini-services, docs) —
# anything listed here must not be imported by src/ (verified: zero imports).
#
# DO NOT add runtime-required paths: src, public, prisma, package.json,
# bun.lock, next.config.ts, tsconfig.json, postcss.config.mjs,
# components.json, next-env.d.ts, eslint.config.mjs.
#
# ⚠ ANCHORING RULE (2026-10-21 production incident — see
# tests/security/route-inventory.test.ts "vercelignore guard"):
#   .vercelignore patterns are gitignore-style: a bare segment name like
#   `audit` matches that name at ANY depth — it silently swallowed
#   src/app/platform/(console)/audit/ (the Super Admin Audit Log page),
#   src/app/api/platform/audit/ and BOTH school-plane audit APIs
#   (src/app/api/homework/[id]/audit, src/app/api/exams/[id]/audit) from
#   every Vercel source upload → those routes 404'd in production while
#   local/CI builds (which never read .vercelignore) stayed green.
#   Every pattern below therefore targets the REPOSITORY ROOT and is
#   written with a LEADING SLASH. Bare un-anchored names are forbidden;
#   the guard test enforces this for every runtime-required file.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# CI-only (GitHub Actions runs the full matrix; Vercel builds never run tests)
/tests
/.github

# documentation-only (ROOT-LEVEL folders only — see the anchoring rule above)
/docs
/audit
/README.md

# local sandbox / operations-only (never imported by the Next.js app)
/mini-services
/scripts
/Caddyfile
/keepalive.mjs
/db

# examples & dev-only tracked files
/.env.example

# local-only artifacts (gitignored already; belt-and-braces)
/.tmp-scripts
/tool-results
/agent-ctx
*.log
